  "paths": "Paths in commands and events are paths on the environment's host, written with forward slashes; never paths of the client's machine.",
  "protocol_version": 1,
  "resume": "Subscribe without since starts from a Snapshot followed by every later Event. Subscribe with since gets exactly the Events after that Seq when the runtime still keeps them in its ring of recent events, otherwise a Snapshot followed by the later Events. A subscriber that falls behind also gets a fresh Snapshot. Events folded into a Snapshot are never sent again.",
  "scopes": [
    "runtime"
  ],
  "title": "Krad ADE runtime protocol",
  "transport": "One byte stream per client (a socket to a cloud runner, or nothing at all in process, where the client calls the runtime handle with the same types). Every frame is length-prefixed; a message frame holds one JSON message, a terminal frame holds raw terminal bytes.",
  "versioning": "protocol_version is the major version. Within it every change is additive: new fields carry a default, new commands, events, messages and codes read as `unknown` on an older peer, which answers a command it does not know with Refused(unsupported) instead of closing. A breaking change raises the major version, and the runtime refuses a Hello of another major version."
